From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:30:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: initialise a station's wcid before publishing it

mt76_sta_add() published the wcid in dev->wcid[] and only then ran
mt76_wcid_init(), so a lookup of that index in between (a late tx
status for the previous user of the index, or an rx frame) saw
uninitialised lists, packet id allocator and phy_idx, and an rx frame
that queued the station for polling had its poll_list entry reset
afterwards. Initialise first; rcu_assign_pointer() orders the stores.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mac80211.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mac80211.c b/mac80211.c
index 361604db..a202c02b 100644
--- a/mac80211.c
+++ b/mac80211.c
@@ -1634,8 +1634,8 @@ mt76_sta_add(struct mt76_phy *phy, struct ieee80211_vif *vif,
 	if (published != wcid) {
 		WARN_ON_ONCE(published);
 		ewma_signal_init(&wcid->rssi);
-		rcu_assign_pointer(dev->wcid[wcid->idx], wcid);
 		mt76_wcid_init(wcid, phy->band_idx);
+		rcu_assign_pointer(dev->wcid[wcid->idx], wcid);
 	} else {
 		wcid->phy_idx = phy->band_idx;
 	}
